 beat is a Triplet with an attached single (888+6) played by my teammate (Previous Player). My only legal move to beat this is a Bomb (7777). Using a bomb against a teammate\'s lead is generally a poor strategy unless I can win immediately (which I cannot with 17 cards) or I need to urgently shift the game state (not necessary here). By passing, I force the Landlord (Next Player) to use resources to beat my teammate or let my teammate continue playing if the Landlord cannot respond. Saving the bomb for the Landlord is critical.\n\nReason: My teammate played the current cards. I should not bomb my teammate\'s hand as it wastes a powerful resource and interrupts their flow. I will pass to let the Landlord attempt to defend or allow my teammate to play again.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
