 the *only* way to avoid guaranteed loss. Even if my teammate *also* has a 2 or a better card, me playing the 2 is still the optimal play.\n\nThus, my plan is clear: I must play the ♠2.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord has only 1 card remaining. The Teammate played a 10. The unknown cards are Q, K, and 2. Any card the Landlord holds (Q, K, or 2) can beat the 10. If I pass or play a card that the Landlord can beat (e.g., J, Q, K, or A if Landlord has 2), the Landlord will play their last card and win the game immediately. I must play a card that guarantees the Landlord cannot play. Since the Landlord might hold the 2 (the highest single), the only safe move is to play my ♠2. This blocks the Landlord 100%. After winning the trick, I can lead my pairs (QQ, KK), which the Landlord cannot beat (since he has only 1 card). If my Teammate holds a pair, we win immediately.\n\nReason: To prevent the Landlord from playing his last card and winning on this turn, I must play a card he cannot beat. The ♠2 is the only card guaranteed to block him regardless of whether he holds a Q, K, or 2.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠2"]}'}
